      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Myocardial blood flow and ventricular function was studied in seven dogs with chronic myocardial ischemia before and after coronary bypass grafting. Restoring blood flow in an area of 25% of the anterior wall of the left ventricle did not significantly improve overall ventricular function. Assessment of intramyocardial pressure as an index of regional myocardial function revealed a consistent enhancement of myocardial contraction at rest, and under pharmacological stress of the heart."},
